1
00:00:00,802 --> 00:00:05,530
EveryMind trains Maryland students, school staff and families to know when to use 988.

2
00:00:05,530 --> 00:00:08,334
Every session ends with a survey, but a spreadsheet

3
00:00:08,334 --> 00:00:10,808
of answers doesn't tell staff what to change.

4
00:00:11,304 --> 00:00:14,061
Our tool turns each survey export into answers.

5
00:00:14,061 --> 00:00:18,167
Save the export, run one command, and it cleans the data, flags labels

6
00:00:18,168 --> 00:00:22,274
it doesn't recognize, codes the comments, and rebuilds this dashboard.

7
00:00:22,274 --> 00:00:24,327
It needs no internet and no coding.

8
00:00:24,781 --> 00:00:26,692
Here are 1,299 responses.

9
00:00:26,692 --> 00:00:30,514
After training, 92% say they know when to use 988.

10
00:00:30,514 --> 00:00:34,948
The biggest jump is describing 988: 46% before, 90% after.

11
00:00:34,948 --> 00:00:41,369
The "before" was asked afterward, so the dashboard flags that gap as an upper bound.

12
00:00:41,831 --> 00:00:43,705
Pick any measure and any group.

13
00:00:43,705 --> 00:00:47,091
Every bar shows how many people it rests on and a likely

14
00:00:47,091 --> 00:00:50,779
range, and groups under ten people are hidden, never guessed.

15
00:00:50,778 --> 00:00:54,466
Students rate the training 7.2 out of ten; school staff, 9.5.

16
00:00:54,466 --> 00:00:58,154
The ranges don't overlap, so that gap is worth a closer look.

17
00:00:58,617 --> 00:01:01,261
Comments are coded offline into themes.

18
00:01:01,261 --> 00:01:05,261
What 988 is was the most valued lesson, in 47% of comments.

19
00:01:05,715 --> 00:01:09,057
And 35% of improvement comments were really questions

20
00:01:09,057 --> 00:01:11,958
about 988, a sign to leave time for questions.

21
00:01:12,416 --> 00:01:17,579
Our top recommendation: only 293 people answered whether they would actually call 988.

22
00:01:17,579 --> 00:01:21,061
Make that question required, and add a short survey at the

23
00:01:21,061 --> 00:01:24,603
start of each session, so next season measures real change.

24
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:28,147
Every number carries an ID that traces back to one

25
00:01:28,147 --> 00:01:31,419
findings file, the same one our memo and slides cite.

26
00:01:31,419 --> 00:01:34,753
Next month: new export, same command, fresh dashboard.
